/0.5 (PR=0.30, ISR/PR=0.65, product=0.195).\n\n**Table 6 (Prolog, 1 seed)**: Exec-only ISR/PR=0.32, Exec+STA ISR/PR=0.58.\n\n**Table 7 (Three-logic summary)**: FOL (0.35→0.65), Prolog (0.32→0.58), SMT-LIB (0.38→0.52). Discriminability: 0.72, 0.45, 0.35.\n\n**Table 8 (Multi-logic training)**: Modest cross-logic benefits. Prolog +0.01 PR from multi-logic. ISR/PR slightly lower under multi-logic.\n\n**Table 9 (Zero-shot cross-logic transfer)**: Positive but small transfer (mean Δ=0.045 over base). STA-trained +0.01 additional Δ vs exec-only.\n\n**Table 10 (SFT baseline)**: SFT PR=0.20, ISR/PR=0.65. GRPO exec+STA PR=0.30, ISR/PR=0.63. SFT gets structure from human demos but lower accuracy.\n\n**Table 11 (4B vs 8B scaling)**: Both scales show ~0.28 ISR/PR gap between exec-only and exec+STA. 8B: exec-only 0.40, exec+STA 0.68.\n\n**Table 12 (Hacking taxonomy, 200 outputs, κ=0.78)**: Exec-only total hack rate 45%, exec+STA 18%, base 25%, SFT 12%. Tautological premises: 18%→3% under STA.\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nAll 12 planned experiments are covered in the paper:\n1. FOL Exec-Only 500-Step Baseline (plan_001) - 3 seeds ✓\n2. FOL Exec+STA 500-Step Primary (plan_002) - 3 seeds ✓\n3. FOL Held-Out Evaluation (plan_003) ✓\n4. O(1) vs O(N) Ablation (plan_004) - 1 seed ✓\n5. Weight Ablation (plan_005) - 1 seed each ✓\n6. Prolog Single-Logic (plan_006) - 1 seed ✓\n7. Multi-Logic GRPO (plan_007) - 1 seed ✓\n8. Cross-Logic Transfer (plan_008) ✓\n9. SFT Baseline (plan_009) ✓\n10. SMT-LIB Single-Logic (plan_010) - 1 seed ✓\n11. Qwen3-8B Scaling (plan_011) - 1 seed ✓\n12. Hacking Characterization (plan_012) ✓\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProduce a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Methodology Soundness** (strengths and weaknesses of the STA formulation, ISR metric, combined reward, 5-step protocol, RIP mapping)\n2. **Experimental Rigor** (statistical robustness, seed counts, ablation coverage, potential confounds, metric validity)\n3. **Reproducibility** (sufficient detail to replicate?)\n4. **Specific concerns or questions** for the authors\n5. **Score** (1-6) with justification\n\nBe thorough, critical, and fair. Identify both strengths and weaknesses. Consider: Are the claims well-supported? Are there missing baselines or ablations? Are effect sizes meaningful? Are there potential confounds? Is the evaluation metric (ISR) well-validated?\n\nOutput your review in structured markdown format with clear section headers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JsSqVCrsrp5pzzVYEXXtj6","session_id":"db36cc0b-3691-41e1-9901-01ea32ffa94b","uuid":"4f93fcae-1683-4ff1-ad05-0cabdf4247e4","timestamp":"2026-05-13T22:27:22.862Z"}
